<StarlightPage
  frontmatter={{
    title: 'Privacy',
    description: 'LaVioLab Atlas, the Claude Code plugin, collects no data. What it runs and where it connects.',
  }}
>
  <p>
    <strong>LaVioLab Atlas collects no data.</strong> The plugin has no server, no telemetry and no
    analytics. Nothing you run through it is sent to LaVioLab or to the author, Stanislav Shupilkin.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-the-plugin-is">What the plugin is</h2>
  <p>
    LaVioLab Atlas (<code>laviolab-atlas</code>) is a set of instructions for Claude Code: three skills,
    <code>start</code>, <code>content-plan</code> and <code>report</code>. It ships no scripts, binaries,
    MCP servers or hooks. It runs on your machine, inside your own Claude Code session, and only when you
    call one of its commands.
  </p>

  <h2 id="where-it-connects">Where it connects</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>The sites you ask it to check.</strong> <code>start</code> and <code>content-plan</code>
      fetch the public pages you name.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google, only if you choose the API route of <code>report</code>.</strong> It reads an
      access token from your own local <code>gcloud</code> login and sends it only to
      <code>searchconsole.googleapis.com</code> and, if you use GA4,
      <code>analyticsdata.googleapis.com</code>. The token is not stored and not sent anywhere else. The
      other route uses a browser you have already connected and are logged into.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    <code>start</code> never installs anything. When the third-party audits it relies on are missing, it
    prints the install commands and leaves the decision to you.
  </p>

  <h2 id="what-anthropic-sees">What Claude and Anthropic see</h2>
  <p>
    The plugin runs inside Claude Code, so what you type and what the commands read passes through your
    Claude session under Anthropic's own terms and privacy policy. The plugin adds no destination of its
    own on top of that.
  </p>

  <h2 id="this-site">This site</h2>
  <p>
    atlas.smolevich.com is a static site. It sets no cookies of its own and has no accounts or forms.
  </p>

  <h2 id="contact">Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions: <a href="https://github.com/Smolevich/pet-project-atlas/issues">open an issue</a> in the
    repository. Source code: <a href="https://github.com/Smolevich/pet-project-atlas">github.com/Smolevich/pet-project-atlas</a>.
  </p>
  <p>Last updated 30 October 2026.</p>
</StarlightPage>
